# Git workflow — feature branch per task

Do **not** implement task work directly on `master`.

## Process

1. Start from the latest `master` (`git checkout master` and update if needed).
2. Create a feature branch for **this task only**, named `feature/<task>` (example: `feature/t3-logger`).
3. Develop and commit only on that branch.
4. Verify before merge: `ruff check .`, `pytest --collect-only`, and `pytest -m framework` (plus any task-specific tests).
5. After verification passes, merge the feature branch into `master`.
6. Do not continue the next task on the same feature branch. Open a new branch from the updated `master`.

## Examples

```text
# ✅ GOOD
git checkout master
git checkout -b feature/t3-logger
# ... implement, test, then merge into master ...

# ❌ BAD
# implement T3 / T4 / docs changes directly on master
# reuse feature/t3-logger for the next unrelated task
```
